  40:  * `{ error: { status, body } }` on any of the three failure modes, which the
  41:  * caller passes straight to `res.status(...).json(...)`. Returning the failure
  42:  * rather than writing the response keeps this usable from anywhere and keeps
  43:  * the status codes defined in exactly one place:
  44:  *
  45:  *   - not a 24-hex string          -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
  46:  *   - well formed, but no seat     -> 404 NOT_FOUND
  47:  *   - seat's office has no rules   -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
